{"nodes":[{"id":"center","type":"text","text":"# ERAM (Shadow Mantle Holder)\n\nSecret boss of the Sword Route in Ch.3, hidden behind the third S-rank minigame of the Original Game. Carries the Shadow Mantle. Fan name taken from his battle theme; in the files he's 'Nightmare'.","x":-180,"y":-70,"width":400,"height":230,"color":"6"},{"id":"s0","type":"text","text":"**Kris**\nSpeaks to them with unsettling familiarity, mocking their possible enjoyment of violence on the game's hidden paths.","x":-130,"y":-538,"width":270,"height":160,"color":"4"},{"id":"s1","type":"text","text":"**FRIEND**\nAppears as a support enemy during his battle — distinct entities, though easy to confuse.","x":346,"y":-209,"width":270,"height":150,"color":"3"},{"id":"s2","type":"text","text":"**Ramb**\nShares the final stretch of the Original Game in the Green Room. Theory: could be Ramb himself after receiving a Shadow Crystal.","x":164,"y":294,"width":270,"height":170,"color":"1"},{"id":"s3","type":"text","text":"**Shadow Crystal**\nHis battle belongs to the same thematic circle as the Shadow Crystals and 'Strange Someone', though he carries the Shadow Mantle, a different item.","x":-424,"y":294,"width":270,"height":170,"color":"3"},{"id":"s4","type":"text","text":"**Is he the 'video game version' of the Roaring Knight?**\nThey share a musical leitmotif, dominant black color, and fire magic.","x":-606,"y":-209,"width":270,"height":160,"color":"1"},{"id":"s5","type":"text","text":"**Is he 'Strange Someone'?**\nThe same one who apparently drove Jevil and Spamton mad — mentions having 'unfinished business' with Kris after the battle.","x":700,"y":150,"width":270,"height":170,"color":"1"},{"id":"s0-img","type":"file","file":"Sprites/kriss_Shadow_Mantle_holder_screenshot.png","x":-136,"y":-933,"width":253,"height":190},{"id":"s1-img","type":"file","file":"Sprites/FRIEND.png","x":705,"y":-367,"width":205,"height":190},{"id":"s2-img","type":"file","file":"Sprites/Ramb.webp","x":413,"y":576,"width":154,"height":190},{"id":"s3-img","type":"file","file":"Sprites/Shadow_Crystal_item.webp","x":-677,"y":563,"width":148,"height":190},{"id":"s4-img","type":"file","file":"Sprites/TheRoaringKnightDeltarune.webp","x":-959,"y":-351,"width":166,"height":190},{"id":"2271c77ca599421d","type":"file","file":"Sprites/Shadow_Mantle_holder_battle_flames.gif","x":-52,"y":-190,"width":114,"height":122},{"id":"s_etim","type":"text","text":"**Etymology of \"Nightmare\"** \"Mare\" comes from a Germanic root meaning incubus/sleep paralysis, not \"mare\" the horse — fitting with \"night\" + Knight. Also, Typer 667 practically encourages Kris to lose against the Knight.","x":-900,"y":50,"width":280,"height":180,"color":"6"}],"edges":[{"id":"e0","fromNode":"center","fromSide":"left","toNode":"s0","toSide":"right","color":"4"},{"id":"e1","fromNode":"center","fromSide":"right","toNode":"s1","toSide":"left","color":"3"},{"id":"e2","fromNode":"center","fromSide":"right","toNode":"s2","toSide":"left","color":"1"},{"id":"e3","fromNode":"center","fromSide":"left","toNode":"s3","toSide":"right","color":"3"},{"id":"e4","fromNode":"center","fromSide":"left","toNode":"s4","toSide":"right","color":"1"},{"id":"e5","fromNode":"s1","fromSide":"right","toNode":"s5","toSide":"left","color":"1"},{"id":"s0-img-e","fromNode":"s0-img","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"s0","toSide":"top","color":"6"},{"id":"s1-img-e","fromNode":"s1-img","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"s1","toSide":"top","color":"6"},{"id":"s2-img-e","fromNode":"s2-img","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"s2","toSide":"top","color":"6"},{"id":"s3-img-e","fromNode":"s3-img","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"s3","toSide":"top","color":"6"},{"id":"s4-img-e","fromNode":"s4-img","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"s4","toSide":"top","color":"6"},{"id":"e_etim","fromNode":"center","fromSide":"left","toNode":"s_etim","toSide":"right","color":"6"}]}